The cannonball is fired from the left and follows a parabolic trajectory. In the sequence, it is shown flying over the ground and heading toward the structures on the right. The trajectory is clearly aimed at the top platform holding robot #4. The cannonball will hit robot #4 first, knocking it off the platform. Robot #4 will fall and likely hit or break the wooden platform it was on, which could cause the platform to collapse. This collapse might also affect robot #2, which is on the same structure. Robot #1 is on a lower level and is unlikely to be affected directly by the cannonball's impact. Robot #3 is on a separate, lower platform and is also unlikely to be hit by the cannonball or affected by the collapse of the structure holding #4 and #2.

After the cannonball hits #4, #4 will be destroyed. The platform it was on will likely collapse, potentially destroying #2 as well. Robots #1 and #3 are not in the path of the cannonball or the falling debris and will remain intact.

